/*Q22.
In a futuristic smart city, there's a network of smart devices with unique functionalities represented by binary flags. Engineers need to combine the functionalities of two devices to create new, advanced features. Write a program to perform the bitwise OR operation on binary codes representing these devices' functionalities.

Input Format:
  - The first line of the input contains the binary code of the first device.
  - The second line of the input contains the binary code of the second device.

Output Format:
  - The output is the integer that represents the device functionalities after performing OR operation.

Note: A partial code is provided in the editor.*/
/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
/*Logic: Same as Q15 with |.*/

import java.util.Scanner;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        long a = Long.parseLong(sc.next().trim(), 2);
        long b = Long.parseLong(sc.next().trim(), 2);
        System.out.println(a | b);
        sc.close();
    }
}
